bilbo remember: keep files or a note as entries, and what changed in them since.

[1mUsage:[22m
  [36mbilbo remember [39m[2m<file|folder>[22m[36m [--kind [39m[2m<kind>[22m[36m] [--tag [39m[2m<tag>[22m[36m]...[39m
                 [--follow]
  [36mbilbo remember - [--tag [39m[2m<tag>[22m[36m]...[39m
  [36mbilbo remember --edit [--tag [39m[2m<tag>[22m[36m]...[39m
  [36mbilbo remember[39m

[1mOptions:[22m
      [1m--kind [22m[2m<kind>[22m  Run this kind, not the one that claims the files
      [1m--tag [22m[2m<tag>[22m    Declare this tag for every entry the run keeps
      [1m--follow[22m       Save the target as a follow in the config file
      [1m--edit[22m         Keep a note written in the editor remember.editor names

[1mKinds:[22m [2mmarkdown, session[22m

[1mOutput:[22m
  new [2m<n>[22m, appended [2m<n>[22m, new generation [2m<n>[22m, unchanged [2m<n>[22m, refused [2m<n>[22m
  records [2m<n>[22m, raw bytes [2m<n>[22m, stored bytes [2m<n>[22m

[1mExit:[22m
  [1m0[22m  success
  [1m1[22m  a refused file or note, nothing to keep, a store, index or editor failure
  [1m2[22m  usage or config error, no editor for --edit, a config --follow cannot write

[1mExamples:[22m
  echo 'The beet seeds are in the drawer.' | bilbo remember - --tag garden

[1mDocs:[22m [2mhttps://github.com/delucca/bilbo/wiki/Commands#remember[22m
